  "question": "Find the exact area enclosed between the curves $y = \\sqrt{x}$ and $y = x^2$ for $x \\geq 0$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Solve $\\sqrt{x}=x^2$.<br /><br />$x^{1/2}=x^2 \\Rightarrow x^4=x \\Rightarrow x=0,1$.<br /><br />Area $=\\int_{0}^{1}(x^{1/2}-x^2)dx$.<br /><br />$=[\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}]_{0}^{1}-[\\frac{1}{3}x^3]_{0}^{1}=\\frac{1}{3}$.<br /><br />Hence area is $\\frac{1}{3}$ square units.",
